  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen has finished strongly, but his approach play is costing him the most strokes. His last ten rounds average 76.0, and his two newest are the best of that stretch: 74 and 71 at the home course qualifier on Sept 25–26. Before that, July tournament scores ran from 73 to 82.\n\n- **Where he loses strokes:** Over the 8 of those 10 rounds that have strokes-gained detail, he averages -6.74 total per round. The two qualifier rounds have no detail.\n  - **Approach:** -4.16 per round, 6th of 7 on the team. The team average is -3.09.\n  - **Off the tee:** -0.32, 6th of 7. The team average is +0.41.\n  - **Putting:** -2.06, 2nd of 7. The team average is -3.03.\n  - **Around the green:** -0.20, 4th of 7.\n- **Total:** His -6.74 puts him 5th of 7, against a team average of -5.79. There is no college figure for strokes gained, and the Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Greens in regulation:** He hit 61.1% over 144 holes. The Division I average is 60%, the team average is 62.8% (5th of 7), and the Tour figure is 66%.\n\nHis last recorded round was Sept 26, so nothing has been logged in about six weeks. The closing qualifier scores are encouraging, but they have no stat lines. I can't tell whether the approach play improved or he scored well another way. The next logged rounds with full stats will show that.",
